def about_page():
    return layout('About','Ming Chen’s research interests, personal background, education, and recognition across cloud systems, AI, robotics, and industry collaboration.',f'''<main id="main"><section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">The person behind the work</div><h1>Curious about ideas.<br>Committed to making them work.</h1><p class="lead">I’m Ming, a computer scientist in Melbourne. I study and build systems that make decisions under changing workloads, incomplete information, and practical resource constraints.</p></div></section>
<section class="page-body"><div class="container about-page-grid"><div class="prose"><p>My route into this work began with robots: speech interaction with a NAO robot, then cloud robotics and real-time multi-robot map fusion at the Chinese Academy of Sciences. Working across sensors, networks, and central computing made the system around a learning method just as interesting to me as the method itself.</p><p>I later led telecommunications and smart-finance R&D projects at SIAT. That experience connected predictive modeling with operational data, industry requirements, and the work of coordinating a technical team.</p><p>During my PhD at the University of Melbourne, I focused on demand prediction and resource management for microservices. I developed forecasting and scheduling methods, implemented research software, and built controlled Kubernetes experiments to examine how those methods behave when conditions change.</p><p>I now work part-time on wearable R&D at CyterX, where data quality, timing, and numerical verification remain central questions. Alongside this, I teach and supervise industry-partner data science projects.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button button-primary" href="/experience/">Experience & collaborations</a><a class="button" href="/cv/">View CV</a></div>
<h2 id="research-interests">The questions I work on</h2><p>{E(DATA['research_profile'])}</p>{research_directions()}
<h2>How I approach the work</h2><div class="working-principles"><div><h3>Start with the decision.</h3><p>Clarify who needs the result, what action it supports, and which constraints matter.</p></div><div><h3>Build something inspectable.</h3><p>Keep configurations, interfaces, data assumptions, and experimental records clear enough for another person to examine.</p></div><div><h3>Evaluate the whole system.</h3><p>Connect algorithm behavior to measurements, implementation costs, and the conditions attached to the conclusion.</p></div></div>
<h2>Education</h2><article class="education-entry"><h3>PhD · Engineering and IT (Computer Science)</h3><p>The University of Melbourne · March 2022–April 2026<br>School of Computing and Information Systems · CLOUDS Laboratory</p><p class="education-thesis">Thesis: <a href="https://clouds.cis.unimelb.edu.au/students/MingPhDThesis2025.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Demand Prediction and Service Scaling Methods for Microservices in Dynamic Computing Environments</a></p><p>Supervisor: Rajkumar Buyya. Co-supervisors: Maria Rodriguez Read and Muhammed Tawfiqul Islam.</p></article><article class="education-entry"><h3>BEng (Hons) · Intelligence Science and Technology</h3><p>Hunan University · September 2012–June 2016<br>Outstanding Undergraduate Thesis.</p></article>
<h2>Selected recognition</h2>{recognition_list()}
<h2>Beyond the keyboard</h2><p>I enjoy tennis, table tennis, pool, and running.</p><div class="personal-interests"><span>Tennis</span><span>Table tennis</span><span>Pool</span><span>Running</span></div></div>
<aside class="profile-panel"><div class="profile-monogram" aria-hidden="true">MC<span>.</span></div><h2>Ming Chen</h2><p class="profile-tagline">Researcher & engineer<br>Cloud and AI systems</p><dl><dt>Based in</dt><dd>Melbourne, Australia</dd><dt>Currently</dt><dd>Data Scientist · CyterX<br>Wearable R&D · Part-time</dd><dt>Education</dt><dd>PhD, University of Melbourne<br>BEng (Hons), Hunan University</dd><dt>Working across</dt><dd>Cloud & edge infrastructure<br>Evidence-based AI<br>Reproducible ML engineering</dd><dt>Email</dt><dd><a href="mailto:{DATA['email']}">{DATA['email']}</a></dd><dt>Elsewhere</dt><dd>{external(DATA['github'],'GitHub')} · {external(DATA['linkedin'],'LinkedIn')}<br>{external(DATA['scholar'],'Google Scholar')} · {external(DATA['orcid'],'ORCID')}</dd></dl><div class="button-row"><a class="button" href="/downloads/ming-chen-cv.pdf" download>Download CV</a></div></aside></div></section></main>''','about')


